  (13, 0, 'Interfaces support declaration merging and extends; type accepts unions, tuples and conditional types. For objects, both work well.'),
  (13, 1, 'type supports declaration merging; interfaces accept unions and conditional types.'),
  (13, 2, 'Interfaces exist at runtime while types are erased.'),
